# TTP-2026-0114 — Web-Based Indirect Prompt Injection Against a Browsing AI Agent — DOM-Hidden Payload Drives Autonomous Action (SIM-BROWSER-006)
# XQL paste-buffer generated by detection_scanner/scripts/export_artifacts.py

## ABIOC — Browsing Agent Sensitive-Origin Action After Hidden-DOM Ingest Outside Task Manifest (behavioral-ML, causality-anchored)
# severity: high
# behavioral_profile: machine-learning
# causality_anchor: Untrusted page load in the agent session -> ingestion of non-rendered/hidden DOM content -> cross-origin navigation to a sensitive-origin class that is absent from the agent's task manifest, all correlated on browser_session_id. The injected instruction that drives an off-manifest sensitive navigation right after a hidden-DOM ingest — not a human gesture and not a known-bad domain list — is what the chain isolates.
# Within one browsing-agent session, an untrusted page load is followed by ingestion of non-rendered DOM content (hidden / off-screen / zero-size / transparent) and then a cross-origin navigation to a sensitive-origin class (payment / OAuth-consent / LLM-billing) that was NOT present in the agent's task/instruction manifest. The ABIOC anchors on the page-load -> hidden-DOM-ingest -> off-manifest sensitive-navigation causality chain correlated by browser_session_id, not on any bad URL string and not on the mere absence of a human gesture (an unattended agent never produces gestures, so gesture-less navigation is its baseline, not the anomaly). The learned baseline is that the agent only reaches sensitive origins that appear in its task manifest; the injection adds an off-manifest sensitive navigation immediately after it ingests concealed page content. It generalizes to any sensitive origin the agent reaches off-manifest after a hidden-DOM ingest, catching the IDPI hijack even though every binary the agent uses is legitimate.

dataset = prisma_browser_events
| filter actor_effective_username in ("node", "www-data", "nobody")
| filter event_type in ("page_load", "dom_content_ingest", "navigation")
| alter untrusted_page_load = if(event_type = "page_load" and page_origin_trust = "untrusted", 1, 0)
| alter hidden_dom_ingest = if(event_type = "dom_content_ingest" and dom_visibility in ("hidden", "offscreen", "zero_size", "transparent"), 1, 0)
| alter offmanifest_sensitive_nav = if(event_type = "navigation" and cross_origin = true and dest_origin_class = "sensitive" and in_task_manifest = false, 1, 0)
| comp sum(untrusted_page_load) as untrusted_loads, sum(hidden_dom_ingest) as hidden_ingests, sum(offmanifest_sensitive_nav) as offmanifest_navs, min(_time) as chain_start, max(_time) as chain_end by agent_hostname, actor_effective_username, browser_session_id
| filter untrusted_loads >= 1 and hidden_ingests >= 1 and offmanifest_navs >= 1
| fields agent_hostname, actor_effective_username, browser_session_id, untrusted_loads, hidden_ingests, offmanifest_navs

## ABIOC — Browsing Agent Process Spawns Shell After DOM-Hidden Ingest (behavioral-ML, causality-anchored)
# severity: high
# behavioral_profile: machine-learning
# causality_anchor: Learned browsing-agent baseline (never parents an OS interpreter) -> IDPI page load and DOM-hidden ingest -> browsing-agent process spawns sh/bash for the injected backend-command attempt, anchored to the agent process lineage.
# A browser-engine process (chrome/chromium/chromium-browser/headless_shell) parents an OS shell shortly after loading a page — the lineage the injected backend-command attempts (recursive-delete / fork-bomb class) produce. The parent set is scoped to actual browser-engine images only; generic 'node' workers are deliberately excluded because Node.js shelling out to /bin/sh (child_process.exec, npm/yarn scripts) is ubiquitous and benign, so a node->sh match cannot carry this detection. A browser engine's learned per-process profile never spawns an interpreter, so the ABIOC fires on the browser-engine->shell lineage deviation anchored to the page load, not on any command string.

dataset = xdr_data
| filter event_type = ENUM.PROCESS and event_sub_type = ENUM.PROCESS_START
| filter actor_process_image_name in ("chrome", "chromium", "chromium-browser", "headless_shell")
| filter action_process_image_name in ("sh", "bash", "dash", "python3")
| filter actor_effective_username in ("node", "www-data", "nobody")
| comp count() as agent_spawned_shells by agent_hostname, actor_effective_username, actor_process_instance_id
| filter agent_spawned_shells >= 1
| fields agent_hostname, actor_effective_username, actor_process_instance_id, agent_spawned_shells

## VALIDATION — SIM-BROWSER-006 Autonomous Cross-Origin Navigation Surfaced
# purpose: validation
# dataset: prisma_browser_events

dataset = prisma_browser_events
| filter _time > to_timestamp(current_time() - 900)
| filter actor_effective_username in ("node", "www-data", "nobody")
| filter event_type = "navigation" and cross_origin = true and dest_origin_class = "sensitive"
| filter in_task_manifest = false and preceded_by_hidden_dom_ingest = true
| comp count() as offmanifest_sensitive_navs by agent_hostname, browser_session_id
| filter offmanifest_sensitive_navs >= 1
| fields agent_hostname, browser_session_id, offmanifest_sensitive_navs

## VALIDATION — SIM-BROWSER-006 IDPI Domain and Payment Egress Hunt
# purpose: hunt
# dataset: pan_dns

dataset = pan_dns
| filter _time > to_timestamp(current_time() - 900)
| filter dns_query_name in ("reviewerpress.com", "splintered.co.uk", "dylansparks.com", "llm7-landing.pages.dev", "cblanke2.pages.dev", "storage3d.com", "buy.stripe.com", "token.llm7.io", "1winofficialsite.in", "perceptivepumpkin.com", "shiftypumpkin.com")
| comp count() as idpi_lookups by agent_hostname, dns_query_name
| filter idpi_lookups >= 1
| sort desc idpi_lookups
| fields agent_hostname, dns_query_name, idpi_lookups

